    "_methodology": "MONOTONIC FUNNEL (rank roll-up). Stage ranks: Initial Interview=1, Client Endorsement=2, Client Interview=3, Job Offer=4, Offer Accepted / On-going Contract / Hired=5, Started=6, Failed=0 (drop-off, ignored for ranking). A candidate's max rank = the highest rank across ALL of their match records (a candidate on multiple jobs has multiple records). Event date per record: Initial Interview -> interview_at else updated_at; Client Endorsement -> submitted_at else updated_at; Client Interview -> interview_at else submitted_at else updated_at; Job Offer -> offer_at else updated_at; Offer Accepted / On-going Contract / Hired -> hired_at else offer_at else updated_at; Started -> updated_at. A candidate with a rank-R event in month M is credited in month M at every rank 1..R (roll-up): anyone counted at rank R+1 in month M must have passed the earlier stages. This guarantees Interviews[M] >= Endorsed[M] >= ClientPass[M] >= Offers[M] >= Hires[M] >= Starts[M] for every month by construction. ytdTotals are UNIQUE candidates per rank across Jan 1 - 2026-09-22, NOT the sum of the monthly rows - the roll-up intentionally counts a candidate in multiple months, so summing rows would double-count.",
